<a class="u-url{% unless lcp %} p-name{% endunless %}" href="{{ page.url }}">{{ title }}</a>
{%- if date %}<time class="dt-published" datetime="{{ date | isoInstant }}">{{ date | humanDate }}</time>{% endif %}
{%- comment %} Task S3 (audit §2.3): <h1 class="p-name primary-title"> moved
to layouts/entry.liquid — the standalone permalink's <article class="h-entry">
wrapper (also moved, to entry.liquid and post-list-entry.liquid, the two
callers) now owns it, so it's the h-entry's title there. This partial no
longer renders inside a title context of its own: when it's the whole page
(entry.liquid sets `lcp`), the h1 already supplies p-name, so this anchor
stays a plain u-url self-link, matching bookmark/like/note/photo/reply below
— when it's a feed-listing entry (post-list-entry.liquid, `lcp` unset), no
h1 exists here at all, so the anchor carries p-name itself, or the feed's
h-entry would have no name. {% endcomment -%}
{%- comment %} Task 18 (§7.4): source (page.liquid:9-11, post.liquid:55-57)
wraps the content div's body in <heading-anchors selector="h2,h3">. h2/h3 is
the source's own choice (its h1 is reserved for the page/post title above,
matching entry.liquid's own <h1 class="p-name"> — content headings start at
h2). IdAttributePlugin (eleventy.config.js) already stamps every heading
with an id server-side; heading-anchors adds the visible anchor link as a
progressive enhancement on top, so the ids work with JS disabled. {% endcomment -%}
<div class="content-grid e-content"><heading-anchors selector="h2,h3">{{ content }}</heading-anchors></div>
